  "body": "Needs maintainer: adds the native camcraft-geometry -> camcraft-kernel dependency (decision file included).\n\nBranch base: upstream/main af83da0f.\n\n## What changed\n- CamCraft opens a Solidcraft `.sc` design as a model. The app reads the cached final body of the design.\n- Model > Open offers `.sc`. A viewport drop takes `.sc`. MCP `import_model` takes `.sc`.\n- These three use the one model import. The `Format::Solidcraft` arm in app dispatches to the re-exported `camcraft_geometry::solidcraft` parser.\n- The module calls `camcraft_kernel::solidcraft::import_solidcraft`. Then it meshes the body with `camcraft_kernel::machining_mesh::machining_mesh` at the STEP chord cap (0.005 mm).\n- A damaged or unsupported `.sc` is refused by name. The message is \"Solidcraft design refused: <kernel reason>\". The model is not added and the history does not change.\n- A watchdog requests cooperative cancellation after 300 seconds. The kernel planner has no cancellation hook. Completion within 300 seconds is not guaranteed.\n- A STEP facet budget for a `.sc` is refused by name, as for STL and OBJ.\n- The kernel edge is native only. The browser build does not offer `.sc`, and it refuses `.sc` by name.\n- `camcraft-kernel` re-exports `CancelToken`, so geometry does not need its own solidcore dependency.\n- Open and drop now use one extension list (`state::MODEL_EXTENSIONS`). The drop refusal message comes from that list.\n- Decision file: `docs/decisions/1456-sc-open.md`. It lists the imported kernel items, why the caller cannot pass the value in, and what rebuilds.\n\n## Review screenshots\n\nBefore uses the production UI files from `af83da0f405cfd244f0c9bf8192ab7309e9db824`.\nAfter uses the production UI files from `8ad6817541bd9acf2c917ed0bc57544aab2bec5f`.\nThe parser move does not change these UI files.\n\nThe native Linux captures call the production `mesh_dialog()` through a temporary test entry point.\nOnly the starting directory is set for the capture. The directory contains the same STL, Solidcraft, and text files.\nThe GTK portal applies the real Mesh filter. Before hides the Solidcraft file. After shows it.\n\n| Picker before | Picker after |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Picker before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/994d7844862ea66d4f2a4fea134a370a75566fb3/2150/picker-before.png) | ![Picker after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/994d7844862ea66d4f2a4fea134a370a75566fb3/2150/picker-after.png) |\n\nThe drop captures render the production shell through the existing egui test harness.\nThe production classifier refuses `notes.txt`. The shell displays that refusal on its status line.\nBefore lists STL, OBJ, STEP, and STP. After also lists SC.\n\n| Drop refusal before | Drop refusal after |\n| --- | --- |\n| ![Drop refusal before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/994d7844862ea66d4f2a4fea134a370a75566fb3/2150/drop-before.png) | ![Drop refusal after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/994d7844862ea66d4f2a4fea134a370a75566fb3/2150/drop-after.png) |\n\nThe images are on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch at `994d7844862ea66d4f2a4fea134a370a75566fb3`.\nNo capture code or images are added to this PR branch.\n\n## Cause\nThe kernel reader from #1464 and #1474 is in main. No code in `crates/app/src` called it. Thus Model > Open did not offer `.sc`.\n\n## Current verification\n\nHead: `13d33b478a7539271fa2ce0a124009f1759c9bd9`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green. Manifest changes select the batch fallback. All 10 steps pass.\n- All-target clippy with `-D warnings` on geometry, app, and UI: green through the gate.\n- Separate kernel clippy with `-D warnings`: green.\n- New geometry pin: `domain_parser_preserves_the_kernel_refusal_reason`.\n- Placement mutation: removing the public geometry module makes the pin fail to compile. Restoring the module makes it pass.\n- Diagnostic mutation: removing the kernel reason makes the new pin fail. Restoring the reason makes it pass.\n- Drop mutation: removing `sc` from `MODEL_EXTENSIONS` makes `a_solidcraft_design_drop_queues_the_import` fail. Restoring `sc` makes it pass.\n- Screenshot evidence check: removing one image link fails the four-image check. Restoring the link makes it pass.\n- The four screenshot URLs return HTTP 200. Their bytes match the local captures.\n\n## Existing import pins\n\n- `crates/app/tests/import_solidcraft.rs`:\n  - `damaged_and_unsupported_sc_files_are_refused_by_name` (debug)\n  - `mcp_import_model_refuses_a_damaged_solidcraft_design_by_name` (debug)\n  - `a_facet_budget_is_refused_for_a_solidcraft_design` (debug)\n  - `the_sample_design_imports_at_its_design_box` (heavy lane, `--release -- --ignored`)\n  - `mcp_import_model_opens_a_solidcraft_design` (heavy lane, `--release -- --ignored`)\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/file_drop.rs`: `a_solidcraft_design_drop_queues_the_import`.\n- Before the initial feature fix, the sample, damaged-file, and MCP pins failed with \"unsupported file type: solidcraft_for_beginners.sc\".\n- Historical sample result: the two heavy tests passed in release in 52 seconds together. They mesh the sample at 0.005 mm.\n- The release heavy tests were not run again for this review fix.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The wasm (browser) build. The wasm32 target is not installed on this machine. The kernel edge is behind `cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\"))`, and the wasm branch of `camcraft_geometry::solidcraft::parse` is a plain refusal.\n- Windows and macOS.\n- Multi-body, assembly, non-mm and other cache versions. The kernel reader refuses these by name. No sample file was available.\n- Clicking Model > Open in the full desktop app. The screenshots call its production picker directly.\n\n## Overlaps\n- #1738 changes `crates/app/src/geometry/import/mod.rs`, `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs` and `crates/ui/src/state.rs`. I did not stack on #1738. It does not change the import functions. This PR changes other functions in those files. Whichever PR merges second refreshes.\n- #2101 adds a field to `Graded` and changes the line that builds it. This PR does not build a `Graded`. It adds a separate match arm and module, so a merge is simple.\n- #2122 adds dependency sections to `crates/app/Cargo.toml`. That is the same file, but a different section.\n- #2091 changes `paint_hint` in `file_drop.rs`. This PR changes other functions in that file.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation).\n\nChangelog: Model > Open, viewport drop and MCP import_model open a Solidcraft .sc design (its cached final body); a damaged or unsupported .sc is refused by name (#1456)\n\nFixes #1456\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
